.TH GIT-CHECKOUTS 1 "2026-07-27" "git-checkouts 0.3.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
git-checkouts \- configure reproducible remote Git checkouts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git-checkouts
.B --host
.I user@host
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git-checkouts
configures a Git remote and remote-side hook that materialize each push as a reproducible worktree.
.PP
The remote layout is:
.PP
.nf
<root>/<forge-host>/<name>/.bare
<root>/<forge-host>/<name>/runs/<run-id>/
<root>/<forge-host>/<name>/latest
<root>/<forge-host>/<name>/LATEST_SHA
<root>/<forge-host>/<name>/deploy-log
.fi
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --host " HOST"
SSH host for the remote checkout.
.TP
.BI --repo " PATH"
Local repository. Defaults to the current directory.
.TP
.BI --name " NAME"
Remote repository folder name. Defaults to the local repository basename.
.TP
.BI --remote " NAME"
Local Git remote name. Defaults to
.B checkouts .
.TP
.BI --root " PATH"
Remote root prefix. Defaults to
.B git .
.TP
.BI --ref " REF"
Push destination ref. Defaults to
.B +HEAD:refs/heads/checkouts/latest .
.TP
.BI --keep-runs " N"
Keep at most
.I N
deploy runs. Defaults to 5.
.TP
.BI --max-run-age " DAYS"
Delete deploy runs older than
.I DAYS .
Defaults to 3.
.TP
.B --force
Replace a different managed local remote URL or hook. Never replaces an unmanaged remote
.B latest
path.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Print planned actions without changing local or remote state.
.TP
.B --json
Emit the result as machine-readable JSON on standard output.
.TP
.B --version
Print the script version.
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Print usage.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Each configuration option has an environment equivalent:
.BR GIT_CHECKOUTS_HOST ,
.BR GIT_CHECKOUTS_REPO ,
.BR GIT_CHECKOUTS_REPO_NAME ,
.BR GIT_CHECKOUTS_REMOTE_NAME ,
.BR GIT_CHECKOUTS_REMOTE_ROOT ,
.BR GIT_CHECKOUTS_PUSH_REF ,
.BR GIT_CHECKOUTS_KEEP_RUNS ,
and
.BR GIT_CHECKOUTS_MAX_RUN_AGE_DAYS .
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
git-checkouts --host user@host --root /scratch/$USER/git
git push checkouts
git-checkouts --host user@host --root /scratch/$USER/git --dry-run --json
.fi
.SH RECOVERY
If a push reports that the remote repository does not exist, rerun the command with
.B --force
and push again. Inspect the deployed commit with:
.PP
.nf
cat <root>/<forge-host>/<name>/LATEST_SHA
ls -l <root>/<forge-host>/<name>/latest
git -C <root>/<forge-host>/<name>/latest rev-parse HEAD
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Configuration or dry-run completed successfully.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid arguments or unsafe option values.
.TP
.B 3
A required dependency or environment prerequisite is missing.
.TP
.B non-zero
The remote setup or push-hook installation failed.
